  "id": "eval.2026-07-28-eval-182510.rag-ingestion-retrieval",
  "title": "RAG Ingestion, Retrieval & Rebuild",
  "description": "# RAG ingestion, retrieval, and rebuild\n\nThe diagram reads left to right across ingestion and query serving. Scheduled or event-driven adapters carry content and ACLs through normalization, content-hash classification, versioned chunking, rate-limited embedding, and an all-stores version gate before publication. Unchanged documents bypass derived processing; parsing, embedding, and partial-publication failures branch to quarantine, DLQ, or repair/rollback paths.\n\nQueries are rewritten into parallel vector and keyword searches, fused and reranked, permission-filtered, and confidence-gated before grounded generation with citations. Thin or low-scoring evidence returns “I don't know,” while feedback captures usefulness and coverage gaps. The lower rebuild lane shows background re-embedding into a consistent new generation, atomic promotion, and retention of the prior generation for rollback.",
  "mode": "diagram",
